rooms_desc ({"  As you enter this room, someone passes you a parka and some skis.  Just a handspan from your feet   is a long sheer cliff dropping severalthousand feet   into endless stretches of snow, rocks, and pine trees. The wind howls around you, blowing fiercely...pushing you over the edge!  You FALL!;;......You land in this room with   a THUD. *phew* Only a nightmare. Or was it?You tracked in snow somehow....","It sure is dark and empty in here... Helloo-oo-ooo.... Echo. Echo.. Echo....It is very dark.","You step through a portal and suddenly realize you've trappedyourself in a glass cage, with the portal as the only obvious exit.Outside the glass, you see an expanse of water and coral reefs,with schools of fish watching you with interest, passing flakes of food to you from high above, where the water does not lap over theedge of the cage. Unfortunately, the walls are too smooth and too highfor you to climb.As you look on, a few angry sharks try to batter the glass, putting a fewcracks in it... water is seeping in... I'd get out of here while I stillcould if I were you.Meanwhile, the rest of the fish seem to be getting a form of nettogether to scoop your corpse out with in the event of your impedingdeath... a giant toilet bowl in the corner seems to be your expectedcoffin....","You have entered Sushi's dojo and excercise room. The floor here is padded-- get those dirty boots out of here!  You see a paper and wood screenopposite you, allowing light into the room, which reveals some bluntedweapons hanging on the wall, a jacuzzi, and a trampoline.","You notice that this is where Sushi does most of her work -- the paint andink flecks on her illustration desk are obvious of that. In front of thedesk is a swivel chair, and next to it is her portfolio, open to a framedpicture of an airbrushed chess board.On a table next to the desk is a radio and a cassette rack, and in the back corners of the room you see an easel, canvases, and art supplies.On one wall is a mural of a green and gold chinese dragon, painted bySushi herself.","	You've just entered Sushi and Gambit's room, which is split into levelsby glass staircases and glass platforms with steel rods running through them. The wall opposite you is sheer glass, revealing a majestic view ofMount Ezo. On the main floor, you hear running water and turn to see acrystalline POOL sparkling in the afternoon light, at the center of a Japanese GARDEN (with a WINTER ROSE in it). A small cascade (WATERFALL)trickles down through the ceiling, splashing the ivy creeping up the wallsbefore it enters a hole in the floor. Somewhere far above the pool, you spota DIVING BOARD on another glass platform.	Curiosity gets the better of you; you climb the clear steps to the highest tier, pull aside a lace curtain, and halt in your tracks... Clearlythis part of the room is off-limits to anyone other than Gambit and Sushi.In front of you is a large waterbed (BED), with black satin sheets and down pillows on it - next to the bed you actually see the outline of anextradimensional DOOR.... Wonder what's in there? Maybe her WARDROBE??Who knows....","You enter a dimly lit room with soft light aimed at the various drawings,airbrushed pictures, ink drawings, and watercolors on the walls. Each painting is of the actual person playing characters in real life. Sushi'sgot a picture of Kevin, Kurt, Brian, Jez, Owen, and Elizabeth here. Youwonder who their characters are....","The walls here are colored a beautiful garnet,  and the room is aptlyfurnished with a t.v., a black leather couch, a stereo, and a halogen lamp.A skylight lights the room brightly.You feel like sitting down and relaxing here...","As you enter the room, a candle on a table lights up and from all around youyou hear the relaxing tones of \"Sweet Lullabye\" by Deep Forest. Your eyesslowly adjust to the dimness of this room and you see several small candleson shelves. A flash of light above you catches your eye and you look up intime to catch a glimpse of a shooting star arc across the night skyoutside the glass ceiling.	In one corner of the room you see a low onyx coffee table with twolarge silk cushions as chairs, and a large candle sits to one side of thetable. The rest of the room looks just as warm and inviting... satin pillows are scattered in one corner and a featherbed mattress lies in another corner.	Things to look at here: Ceiling, table, cushions, pillows, bed,candles, and tea.","Opening the west panels, you step onto the cool green grass in your barefeet. You are in a mud-simulated version of CAUMSETT PARK, a place some-where in another world (the real one) located in Lloyd's Neck, Long Island,NY.	It is a warm spring afternoon, and the opposite side of the potholedpaved trail opens into a wide bowl-shaped field with a *huge* tree at itscenter. Without waiting another second, you dash breathlessly down the hill to the tree, feeling childhood memories of climbing trees return. Whenyou get to the tree, you push the long branches that touch the ground aside,and enter a natural umbrella formed by the tree's outer branches.There is a rope here, leading to a thick branch eight feet above you.Things to look at here: Rope, branch, view, wildlife, swing.",})
rooms_short ({"On Top Of The World","Your Brain","In A Humanbowl","Dojo / Excercise Room","Sushi's Studio","Ezo","Gallery","The Den","Dark Room","Field and Tree",})
